=== nested ROC-AUC (LeaveOneGroupOut, out-of-fold) ===
  1. base rate                0.513  (always-majority accuracy, for reference)
  2. macro-only               AUC 0.505
  3. claim-only               AUC 0.561
  4. claim + macro + derived  AUC 0.588
  5. gradient boosting        AUC 0.573

  DELTA (claim features add, over macro alone): +0.083

  ** macro baseline AUC 0.505 is at/below chance.
     Reading: GENUINE NULL, not an artefact. Across 22 time blocks
     the economy's state at print time carries almost no information about
     whether a forecast came true (every macro feature correlates |r|<0.10).
     So the nested DELTA is not a meaningful 'improvement over macro' --
     but the claim-only AUC (0.561) IS interpretable on its own:
     HOW a forecast is written predicts its accuracy better than the
     economy does. That is the finding.
